*> Implementation test of client/src/args.cob (ARGS-PARSE; contracts/client-surface.md §1): --name
*> is taken as the offline name, --gamedir as the game directory, which defaults to
*> $HOME/.cobolcraft; the order of the options does not matter and other words are ignored.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-ARGS.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLARGS.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-HOME                PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-LEN-EDIT            PIC 9.
 01 WS-OBS-A               PIC X.
 01 WS-OBS-B               PIC X.
 01 WS-OBS-C               PIC X.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     ACCEPT WS-HOME FROM ENVIRONMENT "HOME"
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     INITIALIZE CL-ARGS
     MOVE 2 TO AR-COUNT
     MOVE "--name" TO AR-TEXT(1)
     MOVE 6 TO AR-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE "Alice" TO AR-TEXT(2)
     MOVE 5 TO AR-LENGTH(2)
     CALL "ARGS-PARSE" USING CLIENT-STATE CL-ARGS
     MOVE "args --name Alice gives the name Alice and the game directory $HOME/.cobolcraft"
         TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-EXPECTED TL-OBSERVED
     STRING "Alice|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-HOME) "/.cobolcraft" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-EXPECTED
     STRING CL-NAME(1:CL-NAME-LENGTH) "|" CL-GAME-DIR(1:CL-GAME-DIR-LENGTH)
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     INITIALIZE CL-ARGS
     MOVE 5 TO AR-COUNT
     MOVE "--gamedir" TO AR-TEXT(1)
     MOVE 9 TO AR-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE "build/client-test-dir" TO AR-TEXT(2)
     MOVE 21 TO AR-LENGTH(2)
     MOVE "extra" TO AR-TEXT(3)
     MOVE 5 TO AR-LENGTH(3)
     MOVE "--name" TO AR-TEXT(4)
     MOVE 6 TO AR-LENGTH(4)
     MOVE "Zz_0123456789abc" TO AR-TEXT(5)
     MOVE 16 TO AR-LENGTH(5)
     CALL "ARGS-PARSE" USING CLIENT-STATE CL-ARGS
     MOVE "args --gamedir before --name: both taken, a 16-character name of letters, digits and _"
         TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "Zz_0123456789abc|build/client-test-dir" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING CL-NAME(1:CL-NAME-LENGTH) "|" CL-GAME-DIR(1:CL-GAME-DIR-LENGTH)
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     INITIALIZE CL-ARGS
     MOVE 6 TO AR-COUNT
     MOVE "--generated-dir" TO AR-TEXT(1)
     MOVE 15 TO AR-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE "build/client-test-generated" TO AR-TEXT(2)
     MOVE 27 TO AR-LENGTH(2)
     MOVE "--name" TO AR-TEXT(3)
     MOVE 6 TO AR-LENGTH(3)
     MOVE "Bob" TO AR-TEXT(4)
     MOVE 3 TO AR-LENGTH(4)
     MOVE "--gamedir" TO AR-TEXT(5)
     MOVE 9 TO AR-LENGTH(5)
     MOVE "build/client-test-dir" TO AR-TEXT(6)
     MOVE 21 TO AR-LENGTH(6)
     CALL "ARGS-PARSE" USING CLIENT-STATE CL-ARGS
     MOVE "args --generated-dir <path> sets the generated directory (22 section 5.1), whatever the "
         & "game directory is" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "build/client-test-generated|build/client-test-dir" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING CL-GENERATED-DIR(1:CL-GENERATED-DIR-LENGTH) "|" CL-GAME-DIR(1:CL-GAME-DIR-LENGTH)
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     INITIALIZE CL-ARGS
     MOVE 4 TO AR-COUNT
     MOVE "--name" TO AR-TEXT(1)
     MOVE 6 TO AR-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE "Bob" TO AR-TEXT(2)
     MOVE 3 TO AR-LENGTH(2)
     MOVE "--gamedir" TO AR-TEXT(3)
     MOVE 9 TO AR-LENGTH(3)
     MOVE "build/client-test-dir" TO AR-TEXT(4)
     MOVE 21 TO AR-LENGTH(4)
     CALL "ARGS-PARSE" USING CLIENT-STATE CL-ARGS
     MOVE "args without --generated-dir the generated directory is <game directory>/generated"
         TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "build/client-test-dir/generated" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING CL-GENERATED-DIR(1:CL-GENERATED-DIR-LENGTH) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     INITIALIZE CL-ARGS
     MOVE 4 TO AR-COUNT
     MOVE "--name" TO AR-TEXT(1)
     MOVE 6 TO AR-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE "Bob" TO AR-TEXT(2)
     MOVE 3 TO AR-LENGTH(2)
     MOVE "--world" TO AR-TEXT(3)
     MOVE 7 TO AR-LENGTH(3)
     MOVE "New World (9)" TO AR-TEXT(4)
     MOVE 13 TO AR-LENGTH(4)
     CALL "ARGS-PARSE" USING CLIENT-STATE CL-ARGS
     MOVE "args --world <save folder name> is taken whole, spaces and brackets included" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "New World (9)" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE CL-WORLD(1:CL-WORLD-LENGTH) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     INITIALIZE CL-ARGS
     MOVE 2 TO AR-COUNT
     MOVE "--name" TO AR-TEXT(1)
     MOVE 6 TO AR-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE "Bob" TO AR-TEXT(2)
     MOVE 3 TO AR-LENGTH(2)
     CALL "ARGS-PARSE" USING CLIENT-STATE CL-ARGS
     MOVE "args without --world and CC_WORLD no world is to be opened" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE CL-WORLD-LENGTH TO WS-LEN-EDIT
     MOVE WS-LEN-EDIT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     DISPLAY "CC_WORLD" UPON ENVIRONMENT-NAME
     DISPLAY "Env World" UPON ENVIRONMENT-VALUE
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     INITIALIZE CL-ARGS
     MOVE 2 TO AR-COUNT
     MOVE "--name" TO AR-TEXT(1)
     MOVE 6 TO AR-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE "Bob" TO AR-TEXT(2)
     MOVE 3 TO AR-LENGTH(2)
     CALL "ARGS-PARSE" USING CLIENT-STATE CL-ARGS
     MOVE "args CC_WORLD names the world when --world is absent" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "Env World" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE CL-WORLD(1:CL-WORLD-LENGTH) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   The screenshot run settings of the environment (T4204): CC_SCREENSHOT_AT_FRAME, CC_COMMANDS_AT_FRAME with CC_COMMANDS, CC_SCREENSHOT_THEN_EXIT.
     DISPLAY "CC_SCREENSHOT_AT_FRAME" UPON ENVIRONMENT-NAME
     DISPLAY "7" UPON ENVIRONMENT-VALUE
     DISPLAY "CC_COMMANDS_AT_FRAME" UPON ENVIRONMENT-NAME
     DISPLAY "5" UPON ENVIRONMENT-VALUE
     DISPLAY "CC_COMMANDS" UPON ENVIRONMENT-NAME
     DISPLAY "time set noon;weather clear" UPON ENVIRONMENT-VALUE
     DISPLAY "CC_SCREENSHOT_THEN_EXIT" UPON ENVIRONMENT-NAME
     DISPLAY "1" UPON ENVIRONMENT-VALUE
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     INITIALIZE CL-ARGS
     MOVE 2 TO AR-COUNT
     MOVE "--name" TO AR-TEXT(1)
     MOVE 6 TO AR-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE "Bob" TO AR-TEXT(2)
     MOVE 3 TO AR-LENGTH(2)
     CALL "ARGS-PARSE" USING CLIENT-STATE CL-ARGS
     MOVE "args CC_SCREENSHOT_AT_FRAME, CC_COMMANDS_AT_FRAME, CC_COMMANDS and CC_SCREENSHOT_THEN_EXIT are read" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "7 5 1 time set noon;weather clear" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE CL-SHOT-AT TO WS-LEN-EDIT
     MOVE WS-LEN-EDIT TO WS-OBS-A
     MOVE CL-CMD-AT TO WS-LEN-EDIT
     MOVE WS-LEN-EDIT TO WS-OBS-B
     MOVE CL-SHOT-EXIT TO WS-LEN-EDIT
     MOVE WS-LEN-EDIT TO WS-OBS-C
     STRING WS-OBS-A " " WS-OBS-B " " WS-OBS-C " " FUNCTION TRIM(CL-CMD-TEXT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   Without CC_COMMANDS_AT_FRAME the commands text is not read.
     DISPLAY "CC_COMMANDS_AT_FRAME" UPON ENVIRONMENT-NAME
     DISPLAY " " UPON ENVIRONMENT-VALUE
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     INITIALIZE CL-ARGS
     MOVE 2 TO AR-COUNT
     MOVE "--name" TO AR-TEXT(1)
     MOVE 6 TO AR-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE "Bob" TO AR-TEXT(2)
     MOVE 3 TO AR-LENGTH(2)
     CALL "ARGS-PARSE" USING CLIENT-STATE CL-ARGS
     MOVE "args without CC_COMMANDS_AT_FRAME no commands are set" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE CL-CMD-AT TO WS-LEN-EDIT
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LEN-EDIT) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-ARGS.
